<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khudayar Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1829">1829</a>–<a href="/years/1886">1886</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khudayar Khan was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a>, holding the throne three times between 1845 and 1875 amid civil wars between settled and nomadic factions. Having lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> and much territory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, he became its dependant, and his heavy taxes provoked a revolt in 1875 that drove him into exile. Russian troops then crushed the rebels and annexed the khanate in 1876.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khudayar-khan.jpg" alt="Khudayar Khan" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Commissioned by Konstantin Kaufman, compiled by Alexander Kun · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sayid_Muhammad_Khudayar_Khan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
